  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failure diagnosed: **data-volume disk full \u2014 `No space left on device`**\n\n**What is happening:**\n\n* App `incidentlab-app-1` is running (E1, E7) but `/health` returns 503 `unhealthy` (E2).\n* App logs show health probe failing when trying to write probe file:\n  `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `File \"/app/main.py\", line 116, in health` with `open(probe,\"wb\")` (E6), followed by `GET /health 503` (E6).\n  Earlier `POST /upload 200 OK` then later failure (E6) consistent with volume filling up.\n* Filesystem holding uploads `/srv/lab-data` is 100% used: `size 487.2 MB, used 451.4 MB, available 0.0 MB, use 100.0%` (E4) with inodes only 1.7% used (E4) \u2014 i.e. block exhaustion, not inode exhaustion.\n* That filesystem is bind-mounted into app as `source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw:true` (E7), so app writes fail.\n\n**Ruled out:**\n\n* Permissions: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755`, app user `1000:1000`, `app_user_can_write true` (E5). Parent `/srv/lab-data` same ownership/mode and writable (E11). Not a permission denial.\n* Root disk full: `/` has `use 6.8%, available 91431.1 MB` (E8) \u2014 problem isolated to `/srv/lab-data`.\n* DB dependency failure: `incidentlab-db-1` is `running Up 11s (healthy)` (E1), `health: healthy, running true, OOM false` (E10), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors (E9), `pg_isready exit 0` repeatedly and `health_status: healthy` (E3). App and DB share `incidentlab_default` network (E7, E10).\n* Crash/OOM: App `running true, exit 0, oom_killed false, restart_count 0` (E7). Recent `kill/stop/die/destroy/create/start` at 22:36:37-43 (E3) was a clean recreate of both containers, both now running (E1).\n\n**Root cause vs symptom:**\nRoot cause is disk exhaustion of `/srv/lab-data` (E4). 503 unhealthy (E2) and upload failures with `Errno 28` (E6) are symptoms. DB is healthy (E9, E10, E3) and not the cause.\n\nRepair requires human approval \u2014 free space / expand `/srv/lab-data` volume \u2014 no changes made.\n",
